+      <section id="data-limitations-recommendations">
+        <h2>6) Data Limitations &amp; Policy Recommendations</h2>
+        <div class="grid">
+          <div class="card">
+            <h3>Key limitations (from the dataset structure)</h3>
+            <ul class="small" style="margin: 8px 0 0 18px; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.5">
+              <li><strong>Unbalanced panel:</strong> many countries do not report every year; coverage changes over time.</li>
+              <li><strong>Comparability:</strong> “global” time-series are summaries of reporting countries in that year (not a constant cohort, not population-weighted).</li>
+              <li><strong>Territories:</strong> some territories are separate entries; they may not be comparable to sovereign states and should not be double-counted with parent countries.</li>
+              <li><strong>UK caveat:</strong> the source documentation notes the “United Kingdom” series covers England and Wales only.</li>
+              <li><strong>Age groups:</strong> age-band coverage is much sparser and sex-specific; any age conclusions should be treated as indicative.</li>
+            </ul>
+          </div>
+          <div class="card">
+            <h3>Actionable implications for policy stakeholders</h3>
+            <ul class="small" style="margin: 8px 0 0 18px; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.5">
+              <li><strong>Use robust baselines:</strong> track both median and mean, and report coverage alongside trends.</li>
+              <li><strong>Prioritize male victimization risk:</strong> the sex gap is large and persistent; prevention and enforcement strategies should explicitly address male risk contexts (e.g., street violence, organized crime).</li>
+              <li><strong>Target peak-risk ages:</strong> where age data exist, young adult cohorts (roughly 18–29) show the highest central tendency of rates across countries.</li>
+              <li><strong>Focus on outlier trajectories:</strong> countries with large multi-decade increases or decreases warrant deeper, context-specific review (policy, governance, conflict, criminal markets, policing, public health).</li>
+              <li><strong>Invest in measurement capacity:</strong> improving routine reporting is a prerequisite for credible monitoring and international comparison.</li>
+            </ul>
+          </div>
+        </div>
